course: dictionary
lesson: 6617
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Norwegian is a word with more than one job. Its meaning changes with the words around it. In «Roald Amundsen's Norwegian team», Norwegian describes the team, so it is an adjective meaning from Norway.
explain: When Norwegian stands for a person or a language, it is a noun. «She is a Norwegian» means she is a person from Norway. «Speak Norwegian» means speak the language of Norway. Ask yourself: is the word describing something, or naming a person or a language?
explain: Context clues can help. In «Some zoos keep Antarctic penguins», the penguins are not from Norway, so the word Antarctic tells you the place is cold and far south. Norwegian is different: it is about Norway, a country in northern Europe.
fact: Norway is a country in northern Europe.
fact: As an adjective, Norwegian means from or to do with Norway, as in «Norwegian fjords».
fact: As a noun, a Norwegian is a person from Norway, and Norwegian is also the language spoken there.
fact: The plural is Norwegians, meaning more than one person from Norway.
fact: Vikings came partly from what is now Norway, so Norwegian history is part of the story of the Vikings.
exercise: «Roald Amundsen's Norwegian team reached the South Pole first.» What kind of word is Norwegian here? | A noun, meaning a language | A verb, meaning to travel | A place, like a town | *An adjective, describing the team
exercise: A visitor says, «I am a Norwegian.» What does Norwegian mean here? | A cold, rocky coast | The language spoken in Norway | *A person from Norway | A Norwegian fjord
exercise: Ella says, «Please speak Norwegian.» What is Norwegian here? | A kind of forest | A person from Norway | *The language spoken in Norway | A country in Africa
test: «Edinburgh Zoo's king penguin Sir Nils Olav is an honorary officer in the Norwegian army.» What does Norwegian describe here? | A zoo in Edinburgh | A cold room at the zoo | *The army belonging to Norway | A penguin's food
test: What is the plural of Norwegian when you mean more than one person from Norway? | *Norwegians | Norwegers | Norwegs | Norwegian
exam: Which sentence uses Norwegian as a noun? | We saw a Norwegian forest cat | The Norwegian fjords are long and deep | *Mia is a Norwegian who lives in Bergen | They sailed past Norwegian cliffs
